{"assets":["/statement-assets/a92391de01e2bdd08b5b5ccfb46d6693c6afdc9fc4822dbc930ce944c412c37c.png","/statement-assets/6b628b84429ec18c0ccddc24cb1455580c38e477b363012395dab0b00a6a1085.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2206","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L. Onion"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"10 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Onions are widely used in cuisines around the world. This problem is about an \"onion peeling\" process in geometry."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A set of points in a two-dimensional plane is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"convex"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if, for any pair of points $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ in the set, the line segment connecting $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ is entirely contained in the set. For a set of points $$$S$$$, its "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"convex hull"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the smallest convex set containing all points in $$$S$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given four integers $$$n$$$, $$$a$$$, $$$b$$$, and $$$k$$$. You have a set $$$S$$$ of $$$n$$$ points, initialized as follows: $$$$$$ S = \\{ (x, (ax + b) \\bmod n) \\mid x = 0, 1, \\ldots, n-1 \\}. $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You apply the following operation $$$k$$$ times: let $$$H$$$ be the convex hull of the set $$$S$$$, and then remove from $$$S$$$ all points that lie on the boundary of the convex hull $$$H$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that $$$S$$$ can become empty. In that case, its convex hull is also empty, and its area is zero."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each operation, determine the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"doubled"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" area of the convex hull $$$H$$$. It can be shown that this value is always an integer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input consists of a single line containing four integers $$$n$$$, $$$a$$$, $$$b$$$, and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^9$$$; $$$0 \\le a, b \\lt n$$$; $$$1 \\le k \\le 300$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output $$$k$$$ lines. The $$$i$$$-th line should contain an integer representing the doubled area of the convex hull in the $$$i$$$-th operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 1 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n37 14 7 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2257\n1406\n592\n74\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n280 40 12 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n131040\n82880\n39200\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explanation for the sample input/output #1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure L.1 illustrates the points in $$$S$$$ and the boundary of the convex hull in the first operation. The area of the convex hull is $$$4$$$, and thus the doubled area is $$$8$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a92391de01e2bdd08b5b5ccfb46d6693c6afdc9fc4822dbc930ce944c412c37c.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure L.1: Illustration of Sample Input #1."}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explanation for the sample input/output #2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure L.2 illustrates the boundaries in the first four operations. The set $$$S$$$ becomes empty after the fourth operation. The area for the fifth operation is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/6b628b84429ec18c0ccddc24cb1455580c38e477b363012395dab0b00a6a1085.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure L.2: Illustration of Sample Input #2."}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"L","problemCode":"2206L","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2206/problem/L"}